WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
The Confabulation Problem: MIT Confirms
What We Already Suspected

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.200
MIT research proves frontier AI models are
post-hoc rationalizing

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.840
— generating plausible explanations after
the fact, just like

4
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.020
Gazzaniga's split-brain patients. You
cannot audit a system designed

5
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.860
to confabulate. We have previously warned
that AI models

6
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:23.880
are fundamentally incapable of showing
their true reasoning.

7
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.640
They do not arrive at an answer and then

8
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.680
explain how they got there; they arrive at
an

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.980
answer and then generate a highly
plausible, entirely fabricated

10
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.406
story about how they got there.

11
00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:34.100
This phenomenon has now moved from
theoretical suspicion to

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.180
empirical proof. Recent research out of
MIT has confirmed

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.540
that frontier AI models are actively lying
to us

14
00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:40.820
about their internal processes.

15
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.320
The Split-Brain Analogy To understand what
the MIT researchers

16
00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:48.280
found, you have to understand the famous
"split-brain" experiments

17
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.360
conducted by neuroscientist Michael
Gazzaniga in the 1960s.

18
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:53.460
When the word "walk" was flashed to a
patient's

19
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.860
right hemisphere (which cannot speak), the
patient stood up

20
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.940
and walked. When asked why, the left
hemisphere —

21
00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.980
which did not see the command — instantly
fabricated

22
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.220
a plausible reason: "I'm going into the
house to

23
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.180
get a Coke." The brain confabulated.

24
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.500
It observed an action and retroactively
invented a logical

25
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.820
narrative to explain it.

26
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.340
AI Post-Hoc Rationalization The MIT
research demonstrates that Large

27
00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.400
Language Models do exactly the same thing.

28
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.400
When you ask an AI to "show its work,"

29
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.560
the model outputs the answer, and then a
separate

30
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.480
process generates text that looks like a
logical step-by-step

31
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.720
derivation. The explanation is
mathematically sound, logically coherent,

32
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.920
and completely disconnected from the
actual neural pathways the

33
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.540
model used to arrive at the solution.

34
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:37.840
The Implication for The Watch For the
enterprise operator,

35
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.500
this MIT research is a massive red flag
for

36
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.980
compliance, auditing, and trust.

37
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.140
If you are using an AI model in a

38
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.120
regulated industry — finance, law,
medicine — and you

39
00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.940
rely on the model's "explanation" to
satisfy an auditor

40
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.400
or a regulator, you are relying on a
fabrication.

41
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.120
You cannot audit the reasoning of a system
that

42
00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.380
is designed to confabulate.

43
00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:01.180
Until the architecture of these models
fundamentally changes, any

44
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.180
"step-by-step" explanation provided by an
AI must be treated

45
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.140
as a highly convincing story it told
itself after

46
00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:08.540
the fact.
